# BMW X5 F15 five-door SUV, 2013-2018.
#
# The third X5: the more sculpted body, the connected kidney grille, the
# aerodynamic details and the xDrive four-wheel drive. UK sales from
# 16 November 2013.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BMW_X5_(F15)
#
# Dimensions 4.886 x 1.938 x 1.762 m, wheelbase 2.933 m.
#
# Shape reference: NO true level side profile exists. Image 1 is the most
# side-on view (an sDrive25d); the quarter views show an xDrive40d M Sport
# of the same generation. The flank is estimated; the trim mismatch is
# recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (c), provisional. Black, silver, white and grey are plain
# names. Weights 18, 16, 14, 12, total 60, provisional.
#
# Speed 220 km/h. Comfort 98/477, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 98. Class 3.
# Dates are road presence: 2013 intro, retires staggered 2032-2035.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/bmw-x5-f15.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/bmw-x5-f15.dae. References:
# citycars/references/bmw-x5-f15/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: this is a simplified low-poly interpretation. The flank
# is flat, the shoulder crease and wheel-arch flares are not modelled, and the
# headlamps and grille merge into one dark band in straight-on views. The roof
# runs about 0.1 m further back than the photographs suggest, the rear window is
# short and the painted band above the tail lamps is thick. Mirrors project 4 cm
# per side beyond the published width so that they read. No true side profile
# exists in the pack. At 128 px the tall five-door SUV proportions, joined kidney
# grille and L-shaped tail lamps read as an F15 X5.


